{"result":"{
  "id": "19286",
  "key": "SFCC-796",
  "summary": "Cart Page – Product Unavailable",
  "description": "As a Shopper, I want to be clearly informed when an item in my cart is no longer available, so that I can take action before attempting to proceed to checkout.\n\nThis story covers the UI and behaviour of the cart when one or more line items become unavailable — for example when a product is taken offline or discontinued in SFCC Business Manager while it is still sitting in a customer's bag. It does not cover inventory going out of stock (covered in SFCC-282) — this specifically covers the scenario where the product or variant is no longer active on the storefront but remains in the customer's bag.\n\nThis story covers the interaction between multiple cart components when a product becomes unavailable:\n\n- [SFCC-816](https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-816) \n- [SFCC-404](https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-404) \n- [SFCC-274](https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-274) \n- [SFCC-275](https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-275) \n\nThe key distinction from the OOS state (SFCC-282) is that the Wishlist action is disabled — the customer cannot save an unavailable product to their wishlist as it no longer exists on the storefront.\n\nNote: checkout CTA is enabled \n\n*Designs:* [https://www.figma.com/design/QQ427wHWEUjsjP7H8v48Rs/Zimmermann*Designs?node-id=7580-79309&t=9LWfMTiTVE9jWGsU-4](https://www.figma.com/design/QQ427wHWEUjsjP7H8v48Rs/Zimmermann*Designs) \n\n**Image for Reference:**\n\n![\"image-20260826-021024.png\"](image-20260826-021024.png)",
  "status": {
