    {
      "id": "14211",
      "body": "Hi User:712020:c99d37b3-9c93-4347-951d-5ffb32ff1341 \n\nChecking this particular AC**: Given a line item is in an unavailable state, when the cart renders, then the Remove link remains visible and functional, and the Wishlist link is visible but disabled but visually greyed out,  the customer cannot save an unavailable product to their wishlist as it no longer exists on the storefront.**\n\nIt is clear to me that we can no longer move an unavailable item to the Wishlist if the item itself is no longer available in the storefront. However, I wanted to clarify the scenario where the product is expected to come back in stock *(Meaning it’s just out of stock but still enabled on the storefront.)*\n\nWe currently have functionality that allows customers to add the unavailable product to their Wishlist, and once it is back in stock, the customer is notified that it is available again.\n\nCould you please confirm if this functionality is still part of the SFCC implementation, or if it is covered under a different Jira story?\n\nThanks,\n\nKim\n\ncc User:600810992b411b0076aaf4cc",
      "author": {
        "display_name": "Kim Simbulan",
        "name": "Kim Simbulan",
        "email": null,
        "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/6cbe89def4f1ebaf2e97714883223299?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FKS-0.png"
      },
      "created": "2026-09-02T10:11:40.805+1000",
      "updated": "2026-09-02T10:11:57.924+1000"
    },
    {
      "id": "14212",
      "body": "Hi User:61f1c44458ce4f006895680f \n\nThat use case is only valid for OOS items and is covered in another story; if a product is removed from the website because it is not longer a sellable product then a client should not be able to add it to the wishlist.\n\nI hope this is clear.\n\nccUser:600810992b411b0076aaf4cc User:557058:09af9e5b-661b-42a2-90ec-9ce9f69d324d",
